
Usage: gitpak <command> [flag]

A package manager for ensuring software from git stays up to date

Flags:
    --help, -h          Show help info
    --version, -v       Print the version info

Commands:
    install ,in <url(s)> :
        Install a package by the git URL by setting instructions 

        --no-clone :  
            Will not perform a git clone at the start of installation; useful for specific situations 
            e.g. using gh to download from releases section
            #in progress

    force-install, fi <name(s)> :
        Installs the package regardless of whether it needs updating
    
    remove, rm <name(s)> :
        Remove a package from gitpak (Does not uninstall package!!!)

    update, up :     
        Update installed packages
    
    list-updates, lu :
        List packages which need updating
    
    ######### not done yet ########
    add-lock, al :
        Lock the package at the current version

    remove-lock, rl :
        Remove the package lock
    ###############################
    
    list :
        List installed packages